From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:44:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: mediatek: mt6797: set the AFE up again after a system
 suspend

The AFE takes a runtime PM reference at probe and keeps it, so runtime
PM never stops it. A system suspend still powers its AUDIO domain off:
genpd counts every device in the domain as suspended and turns the
domain off at suspend_noirq. The AFE comes back from reset, while the
driver still takes it for running and configured. On the Gemini the
first stream after resume failed with "hw_ptr err", until the driver
was reloaded.

Use the common mtk_afe_suspend() and mtk_afe_resume() as the DAI
component's callbacks, as mt8173 does. They run the runtime suspend and
resume, which stop the AFE and set up its interrupt and memory
interface defaults again. No register needs saving: every AFE control
is a DAPM control, which DAPM writes again when the next stream powers
its path.
---
 sound/soc/mediatek/mt6797/mt6797-afe-pcm.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/mediatek/mt6797/mt6797-afe-pcm.c b/sound/soc/mediatek/mt6797/mt6797-afe-pcm.c
index 1c759822f..3e47c6937 100644
--- a/sound/soc/mediatek/mt6797/mt6797-afe-pcm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/mediatek/mt6797/mt6797-afe-pcm.c
@@ -385,8 +385,16 @@ static const struct snd_soc_dapm_route mt6797_memif_routes[] = {
 	{"UL_MONO_2_CH1", "ADDA_UL_CH2", "ADDA Capture"},
 };
 
+/*
+ * The AFE stays runtime active, but a system suspend still powers its AUDIO
+ * domain off once every device in it has suspended, which resets the AFE.
+ * Stop it before and set it up again after, as runtime PM would. Every AFE
+ * control is a DAPM one, so DAPM rewrites the routing at the next stream.
+ */
 static const struct snd_soc_component_driver mt6797_afe_pcm_dai_component = {
 	.name = "mt6797-afe-pcm-dai",
+	.suspend = mtk_afe_suspend,
+	.resume = mtk_afe_resume,
 };
 
 static const struct mtk_base_memif_data memif_data[MT6797_MEMIF_NUM] = {
-- 
2.43.0

